[126.457978, "o", "\"stdout\":\"APP0000001DENY  INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\\nAPP0000002APPRO\\n001 00002316.70 00002291.66 00000025.03 0000004974.96\\n002 00002316.70 00002280.19 00000036.51 0000004938.44\\n003 00002316.70 00002263.45 00000053.24 0000004885.20\\n004 00002316.70 00002239.05 00000077.65 0000004807.54\\n005 00002316.70 00002203.46 00000113.24 0000004694.30\\n006 00002316.70 00002151.55 00000165.14 0000004529.15\\n007 00002316.70 00002075.86 00000240.84 0000004288.31\\n008 00002316.70 00001965.47 00000351.22 0000003937.09\\n009 00002316.70 00001804.50 00000512.20 0000003424.88\\n010 00002316.70 00001569.74 00000746.96 0000002677.92\\n011 00002316.70 00001227.38 00001089.32 0000001588.60\\n012 00002316.71 00000728.11 00001588.60 0000000000.00\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[137.651274, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_0135xfC1szsaPVTxuAJxp9na\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The interest is very high (2291.66 on 5000 loan). Let me reconsider - the rate \\\"00550\\\" with 9(3)V9(2) means 005.50. But maybe this is meant to be 5.50% annual rate, not 550%! Let me check:\\n\\n5000 * 5.5 / 1200 = 22.92 ✓ This matches the expected interest!\\n\\nSo the issue is my calculation is treating 005.50 as the full value, but with 9(3)V9(2) that would be 5.50, and dividing by 1200 gives 0.00458... but somehow I'm getting the wrong result.\\n\\nWait - I think the issue is that 9(3)V9(2) means the V is an implied decimal. So \\\"00550\\\" actually represents 005.50, but when COBOL reads it without explicit decimal handling, it might be treating it as 55000 or similar.\\n\\nLet me check how the rate is being parsed:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":575,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":"]
