[137.890747, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_0135xfC1szsaPVTxuAJxp9na\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01YYN8fA1jXZK61hpv1wYs1M\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cat /app/src/INPUT.DAT\",\"description\":\"View input data again\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":575,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":24474,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":575,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0c356a6e-3a6b-4a08-ac27-53910b574c21\",\"uuid\":\"4f4d68db-d5ed-4283-a3e2-c0d5edf6cc7c\"}\r\n"]
[138.404057, "o", "{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01YYN8fA1jXZK61hpv1wYs1M\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"APP0000001;Williams David Robert         ;2000000000;3500000000;0500000000;20;00550\\nAPP0000002;John Smith Clark              ;0000005000;0000004000;0000003500;01;00550\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0c356a6e-3a6b-4a08-ac27-53910b574c21\",\"uuid\":\"ca93c78e-eddf-490b-baa7-87168ea462cb\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"APP0000001;Williams David Robert         ;2000000000;3500000000;0500000000;20;00550\\nAPP0000002;John Smith Clark              ;0000005000;0000004000;0000003500;01;00550\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[149.847085, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01Rey2MGb5aQnGRGK2NrSDPC\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Looking at the parsing, the rate \\\"00550\\\" with PIC 9(3)V9(2) should be interpreted as 005.50 (5.50%). The monthly rate should be 5.50/1200 = 0.00458333.\\n\\nFor loan 5000 at 0.458333% monthly for 12 months:\\n- Monthly payment = 5000 * 0.00458333 / (1 - 1.00458333^-12) = 428.04\\n\\nBut expected shows 400. Let me check if the example is showing a specific scenario or if there's another interpretation. Actually, looking more carefully at the expected output:\\n- Payment = 400.00\\n- Interest = 22.92 (which is 5000 * 0.004583 = 22.92) ✓\\n- Principal = 377.08 (400 - 22.92 = 377.08) ✓\\n- Remaining = 4622.92 (5000 - 377.08 = 4622.92) ✓\\n\\nSo if payment is 400, the math works. But annuity formula would give ~428 for 12 months. Maybe the example uses a different calculation approach or different parameters.\\n\\nLooking again at the input - maybe t"]
[149.847139, "o", "he LOAN_AMOUNT after deducting DOWN_PAYMENT?\\n- Loan = 5000, Down = 3500, Net Loan = 1500? No, that doesn't fit either.\\n\\nActually, looking at the raw numbers in the issue description example again - the values in the example output may just be illustrative. Let me verify my calculation is correct with proper annuity formula and see if the program is working correctly.\\n\\nThe issue I see is that the interest (2291.66) is way too high. 5000 * 5.5 / 1200 = 22.92, not 2291.66. So the rate is being interpreted incorrectly. The rate is coming as 550 (integer part) instead of 5.50.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":393,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":25049,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":393,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0c356a6e-3a6b-4a08-ac27-53910b574c21\",\"uuid\":\"35cd9515-c691-48fb-b04d-f6010ab82fe3\"}\r\n"]
