[176.173459, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01DUAdAguReMXQBYZWASp84X\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the interest part (22.91) is close to the expected 22.92 (small rounding difference). The payment is 429.18 which is the correct annuity payment for a 5000 loan at 5.5% annual for 12 months.\\n\\nLet me verify:\\n- Monthly rate = 5.5/1200 = 0.0045833\\n- 5000 * 0.0045833 / (1 - 1.0045833^-12) = 429.18 ✓\\n\\nThis is mathematically correct! The example output showing 400.00 was probably just illustrative and not based on real calculations.\\n\\nLet me check if the output format matches the expected format exactly:\\n- Expected: `TEST000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT`\\n- Got: `APP0000001DENY  INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT` (has extra space after DENY)\\n\\nLet me fix the format:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":472,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":28232,\"cache_creation\":"]
